msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:213
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Copy CD in Safe Mode:</b> In this mode process will first read out "
"source CD as an image file(s) to your hard drive and then burn it to target "
"CD-R(W). This mode decreases chance of buffer underruns. Working directory must "
"have sufficient space available to store image file(s). If not sure, use this "
"mode."
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:217
msgid "Copy CD in Fast Mode"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:218
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Copy CD in Fast Mode:</b> Perform CD copy on the fly without creating an "
"image file. Success of such copy depends on your machine capabilities and "
"system load. Higher system load especially on weaker machines increases "
"possibility of failure due to buffer underruns. This is however the fastest way "
"to copy CD."
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:227
msgid "Force Copy"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:228
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Force Copy:</b> In this mode process will try to read out source Data CD "
"even on some errors. Use when Safe and Fast modes fail."
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:230
msgid "Test Force Mode"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:233
msgid "Copy CD in Track-at-Once Mode"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:234
msgid "Test Track-at-Once Mode"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:235
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Copy CD in Track-at-Once Mode:</b> Will append tracks to an empty "
"CD-R(W) or an existing Audio CD in Track-at-Once Mode. If not finalized, it "
"will be possible to add Tracks to such CD at a later time (provided there is "
"enough space left). However, CD Text can not be added and CD layout can not be "
"manipulated. To append to an existing Audio CD it must itself be in "
"Track-at-Once Mode and not finalized (fixated)."
msgstr ""

